  "answer": "NovaLearn should prioritize the regulated mid-market and enterprise customer segments [NL-012#NL-012-S09]. This is supported by the official metrics and customer success reports showing that these segments deliver the strongest business opportunity for the following reasons:\n\n- **Lower churn and higher stability**: Mid-market accounts have a monthly logo churn of 2.1%, and enterprise accounts just 1.3%, compared to 4.8% for the SMB segment [NL-016#NL-016-S03], [NL-012#NL-012-S09].\n- **Revenue and expansion strength**: Mid-market and enterprise customers combined generate 83.8% of recurring revenue, and together they recorded $155,000 in expansion revenue versus only $18,000 for SMB [NL-016#NL-016-S03], [NL-012#NL-012-S09].\n- **Higher customer satisfaction**: Enterprise NPS is 52 and Mid-Market NPS is 47, far exceeding the SMB NPS of 31 [NL-012#NL-012-S08], [NL-016#NL-016-S01].\n- **Superior unit economics**: The enterprise segment achieves an LTV:CAC ratio of 16.0x compared to just 8.3x for SMB [NL-016#NL-016-S03].\n- **Strategic market fit**: The common denominator among these high-performing accounts is regulatory compliance and heavy documentation, where NovaLearn has a distinct competitive advantage [NL-016#NL-016-S03]. This has prompted the strategic shift of outbound sales focus entirely away from SMBs [NL-016#NL-016-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
